course: dictionary
lesson: 5331
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. A keyhole is the small hole in a lock where you put the key. «Dad caught Ben at the keyhole looking at hidden presents» means Ben was peeping through that hole, not that he had a key in his hand.
explain: Check the clues around the word. Who is at the keyhole, and what are they doing? Ben is looking at hidden presents, so the keyhole is a place to look through. Then put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: The same word can also come before another word, as in keyhole surgery. «Keyhole surgery uses small cuts and a camera» tells you that the operation is done through tiny cuts, not one big opening. Here keyhole describes the kind of surgery, and the clues are small cuts and a camera.
fact: A keyhole is the small hole in a lock where you put the key.
fact: Keyhole surgery is an operation done through very small cuts, using a camera.
fact: In keyhole surgery, the camera lets the doctor see inside the body without one big cut.
fact: Keyhole surgery usually means quicker healing and smaller scars, as the sentence about appendix operations shows.
fact: A word can have more than one meaning, so always check the words around it.
exercise: «Dad caught Ben at the keyhole looking at hidden presents.» Where was Ben standing? | Opening a window | *Peeping through the hole in a lock | In the garden | Under the Christmas tree
exercise: «Keyhole surgery uses small cuts and a camera.» What does keyhole describe here? | A hole in the wall | A lock on a door | *The kind of surgery done through tiny cuts | A big cut in the skin
exercise: «They lock him in his bedroom, while Toad shouts rude names through the keyhole.» Where is Toad? | Inside the bedroom with him | *Outside the locked door, talking through the hole in the lock | In the kitchen making tea | Under the bed
test: Keyhole surgery is done through very small cuts. What does keyhole surgery mean? | *An operation through tiny cuts, using a camera | A big operation with long scars | A surgery done at the keyhole of a door | A holiday for doctors
test: Ben put the key in the keyhole. What is a keyhole? | A sort of window | *The small hole in a lock where you put the key | A big hole in the floor | A hole in the wall for letters
exam: Jayden says keyhole surgery means a big cut and a long stay in hospital. What do the clues show? | *Jayden is wrong: small cuts, a camera and quicker healing | Jayden is right, because keyhole means big cuts | Keyhole surgery is only for fixing locks | Keyhole surgery is the same as looking through a door
